I merged PR #253 from @rbuss93 and published it as **version 295.0**. It fixes three places that kept Visual Studio's own colors when the extension is set to a forced Dark, Light or Custom theme, which made them unreadable:
- the dropdown menus, plus the chat's effort and usage popups;
- the user's own prompt bubble in the chat;
- the title bar of the Session History, Rename Session and Resume Conversation dialogs.

I haven't checked any of these in a running Visual Studio.

- **Review:** the change is safe: no network calls, no new dependencies, no build-script changes. It is small (one override list, one dialog helper) and adds tests that catch any panel color the forced theme misses.
- **Testing:** the Release build succeeded and all 1050 unit tests passed, both on the PR branch and on master after merging. `publish.cmd` reported a successful upload to the Marketplace.
- **Follow-up on master (774330c), with no change to the contributor's code:**
  - version bump to 295.0;
  - a README release note with the credit line;
  - @rbuss93's count in the contributors list raised from 9 to 10 PRs;
  - updated Theme and dialog notes in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
- **PR and issue:** I posted a thank-you comment on the PR, which is merged and closed. Issue #252 was opened by the same contributor and GitHub closed it on merge; I commented there that the fix is released in 295.0.
